# Context Menu System Implementation Checklist

Status: planned

## Goal

Add a reusable DwarfUI context-menu system whose registration and target
resolution resemble the existing tooltip system while providing synchronous
right-click ownership and an interactive menu.

A caller registers a small `ContextMenuDefinition` against either a UI widget
or an exact map tile. Right-clicking an eligible registered target opens one
menu and consumes the complete opening gesture. UI-widget menus are anchored
to the captured screen position. Map-tile menus retain their world position
and are reprojected before every render so they remain attached while the map
viewport moves.

## Locked product decisions

- [ ] All context-menu-owned production modules live under
      `src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/context_menu/`.
- [ ] All focused unit and DwarfSpec files live under
      `tests/context_menu/`.
- [ ] The public facade is loaded with
      `reqscript('dwarfui/context_menu/api')`; do not add a top-level
      `dwarfui/context_menu.lua` compatibility facade.
- [ ] A UI-widget registration opens at the screen position captured from the
      opening right-click.
- [ ] A map-tile registration opens from an exact world tile and recomputes
      its projected screen position before every render.
- [ ] "Screen position" means the DFHack screen/interface coordinate space
      used by widget frames, mouse input, and interface painting. It does not
      mean an operating-system physical display pixel.
- [ ] Screen-position anchors remain fixed for the open session, apart from
      menu-frame reclamping after an interface-size change.
- [ ] Map-tile anchors move with camera panning and zoom and close when the
      source tile is no longer projectable on the displayed z-level or inside
      the visible map viewport.
- [ ] Opening on a registered target consumes every delivered boundary of the
      right-click gesture so native DF and other UI cannot also react.
- [ ] `LEAVESCREEN`/Escape closes the open menu and consumes the input.
- [ ] A second right-click closes the open menu and consumes the complete
      right-click gesture without reopening another target.
- [ ] Left-clicking an entry closes the menu, consumes the input, and invokes
      that entry exactly once.
- [ ] Left-clicking outside the menu closes it and consumes the complete
      delivered click gesture.
- [ ] Selecting an entry by keyboard also closes before invoking its handler
      and consumes the selection input.
- [ ] The definition used by an open menu is a validated snapshot. Updating a
      registration affects its next opening, not the current session.
- [ ] Entry colors resolve independently in this order: entry override,
      menu-level default, system default.
- [ ] The initial system uses `COLOR_WHITE` as the system foreground default
      and `COLOR_BLACK` as the system background default.
- [ ] UI-widget targets take precedence over map-tile targets. A blocking UI
      region suppresses map fallback even when that region has no context
      menu.
- [ ] The menu closes before calling `on_select` so handler errors, reloads,
      or reentrant menu operations cannot leave stale presentation state.
- [ ] Context-menu presentation may own focus and input while open. It does
      not inherit the tooltip requirement to remain transparent to focus and
      input.
- [ ] No implementation or test may rely on loose discriminator strings or
      magic numbers. Closed sets use immutable numeric LuaDoc enums and named
      members.
- [ ] Every new or modified class and method has LuaDoc documentation.
- [ ] Local unit evidence, packaged-module evidence, registered live-runtime
      evidence, and manual visual evidence are recorded separately.

## Intended public contract

```lua
local context_menu = reqscript('dwarfui/context_menu/api')

context_menu.register(widget, {
    title='Route stop',
    fg=COLOR_WHITE,
    bg=COLOR_BLACK,
    entries={
        {
            label='Move stop',
            on_select=function(context)
                -- Update the selected stop.
            end,
        },
        {
            label='Delete stop',
            fg=COLOR_LIGHTRED,
            on_select=function(context)
                -- Delete the selected stop.
            end,
        },
    },
})

local handle = context_menu.register_map_tile{
    owner=overlay,
    pos=stop.pos,
    definition=definition,
}
```

The implementation may expose explicit `update(widget, definition)`,
`unregister(widget)`, and atomic
`update_map_tile(handle, {pos=pos, definition=definition})` operations. It
should not require callers to mutate a registered definition table by side
effect.

## Planned module layout

```text
src/scripts_modinstalled/dwarfui/
  context_menu/
    api.lua
    definition.lua
    input_hook.lua
    map_target.lua
    registration.lua
    renderer.lua
    screen.lua
    service.lua
    target_detector.lua
    target.lua
```

If map projection is extracted as reusable infrastructure, its generic module
may live outside this directory. The context-menu-owned adapter, session
logic, and tests must remain inside their dedicated directories.

## Phase 0 - Freeze runtime seams and the API contract

- [ ] Record the active DwarfUI revision, branch, and worktree state before
      implementation.
- [ ] Record the active DFHack version and source revision used to audit input,
      `gui.ZScreen`, overlay, widget, and viewport behavior.
- [ ] Trace the current tooltip registration, root resolution, target
      detection, weak ownership, reload, and map-target behavior and identify
      the exact contracts to reuse.
- [ ] Confirm that tooltip pointer polling is not an opening-input seam because
      it runs after input and cannot consume a right-click.
- [ ] Verify the native input contract from
      `plugins.overlay.feed_viewscreen_widgets()` through the C++ overlay feed
      hook, including the meaning of a truthy Lua return.
- [ ] Verify the effective `onInput()` seam for Lua `gui.Screen` and
      `gui.ZScreen` instances, including predecessor call and return behavior.
- [ ] Record which right-click keys the active DFHack build can deliver,
      including `_MOUSE_R_DOWN` and `_MOUSE_R`.
- [ ] Record which left-click keys the active DFHack build can deliver so an
      outside close cannot leak a trailing boundary.
- [ ] Verify `gui.ZScreen` parent render, focus, dismissal, pause, movement,
      and `sendInputToParent()` behavior.
- [ ] Verify native `widgets.List` keyboard, mouse, wheel, selection, and
      submission behavior and identify which row-painting behavior requires a
      context-menu-specific renderer.
- [ ] Audit the existing minecart world-to-interface projection in text and
      Premium graphics modes and decide whether to extract a generic helper or
      consume an existing public helper.
- [ ] Define immutable numeric `ContextMenuTargetKind` members for
      `WIDGET` and `MAP_TILE`.
- [ ] Define immutable numeric `ContextMenuAnchorKind` members for
      `SCREEN_POSITION` and `MAP_TILE`.
- [ ] Keep target identity and anchor placement as separate concepts throughout
      the API and internal session model.
- [ ] Specify whether any explicit programmatic `open_at_*` API is needed by
      an initial consumer. Do not publish convenience entry points without a
      concrete use case and tests.

### Phase 0 completion gate

- [ ] The opening, closing, consumption, rendering, and projection seams are
      supported by the active DFHack source rather than assumptions.
- [ ] The public registration contract and both anchor modes are written down
      before production modules are added.
- [ ] Any deviation from the architecture in this checklist is recorded in
      this planning document before implementation proceeds.

## Phase 1 - Implement definitions, snapshots, and open-session types

- [ ] Add `context_menu/definition.lua` with documented
      `ContextMenuDefinition` and `ContextMenuEntry` annotations.
- [ ] Support an optional non-empty title after validation.
- [ ] Support menu-level optional `fg` and `bg` colors.
- [ ] Require a non-empty `entries` list.
- [ ] Require every entry to contain a non-empty string `label`.
- [ ] Require every entry to contain a callable `on_select`.
- [ ] Support independent optional entry-level `fg` and `bg` colors.
- [ ] Reject unknown shapes and invalid values with errors that identify the
      offending field and entry index.
- [ ] Resolve missing colors through entry, menu, and system defaults without
      mutating the caller's table.
- [ ] Snapshot title, resolved pens, labels, and handler references when the
      menu opens.
- [ ] Add documented target and anchor descriptor types in
      `context_menu/target.lua`.
- [ ] Define a documented selection-context object containing target kind,
      anchor kind, source widget or map owner identity, source root, captured
      screen position, and copied map position where applicable.
- [ ] Never retain a native map object pointer when a copied coordinate or
      stable numeric identity is sufficient.
- [ ] Add a documented open-session type that owns exactly one definition
      snapshot, target descriptor, anchor descriptor, and lifecycle state.
- [ ] Add focused definition tests under `tests/context_menu/` for valid,
      invalid, empty, and partially colored definitions.
- [ ] Add focused snapshot tests proving caller mutation after opening does not
      alter the active menu.

### Phase 1 completion gate

- [ ] Definition validation, color fallback, snapshot immutability, enum use,
      and selection context are deterministic without a live DF runtime.
- [ ] Every new class and method has LuaDoc documentation.

## Phase 2 - Implement widget and map-tile registration

- [ ] Add `context_menu/registration.lua` as the owner of public widget
      registrations and registration lifecycle.
- [ ] Preserve tooltip-like weak widget ownership so registration does not
      keep a removed widget alive.
- [ ] Make repeated registration of the same widget deterministic and
      idempotent for the same definition.
- [ ] Implement explicit widget update and unregister behavior.
- [ ] Resolve the widget's eligible current root dynamically instead of
      retaining a stale screen or overlay root.
- [ ] Reject detached, hidden, inactive, disabled-overlay, foreign-root, or
      otherwise ineligible widget registrations at target-resolution time.
- [ ] Add `context_menu/map_target.lua` with exact copied x/y/z keys, weak
      owner semantics, and disposable registration handles.
- [ ] Define deterministic latest-registration precedence for duplicate map
      coordinates.
- [ ] Implement atomic map-handle updates for position and definition.
- [ ] Ensure a failed update leaves the prior map registration intact.
- [ ] Automatically remove map registrations when their weak owner or handle
      is no longer live.
- [ ] Start any registration-gated input/root discovery only when at least one
      eligible registration exists.
- [ ] Stop discovery and release hooks when the final registration disappears
      and no menu is open.
- [ ] Add focused registration tests for collection, detach, visibility,
      root changes, disabled overlays, duplicate map positions, failed updates,
      explicit unregister, and reload generation changes.

### Phase 2 completion gate

- [ ] Widget and map registrations have weak, reload-safe, explicitly tested
      ownership.
- [ ] Registration alone does not open a screen, consume input, or mutate a
      consumer root.

## Phase 3 - Implement target detection and anchor capture

- [ ] Add `context_menu/target_detector.lua` and reuse the generic
      `dwarfui/pointer` traversal policies instead of creating a second widget
      hit tester.
- [ ] Traverse overlapping UI descendants in reverse render order.
- [ ] Preserve `target`, `pass`, `block`, and `none` policy semantics.
- [ ] Allow only a currently eligible registered widget to resolve as a widget
      context-menu target.
- [ ] Suppress map fallback when pointer traversal reports a blocking UI
      region, including native UI occluding the map.
- [ ] Attempt exact same-z map lookup only after widget resolution reports a
      true miss rather than a block.
- [ ] Give a widget target precedence over a map target at the same screen
      position.
- [ ] Capture the opening pointer position as a copied
      `SCREEN_POSITION` anchor for a widget target.
- [ ] Capture the registered copied world coordinate as a `MAP_TILE` anchor for
      a map target.
- [ ] Preserve the source root and stable target identity in the selection
      context without extending their lifetime unnecessarily.
- [ ] Do not infer a map target from a projected marker, label, or proximity;
      resolve the exact world tile under the pointer.
- [ ] Add focused tests for overlap, clipping, target ownership, blockers,
      UI-over-map precedence, exact same-z matching, duplicate map entries, and
      both anchor descriptor types.

### Phase 3 completion gate

- [ ] One pointer sample produces exactly one eligible target, block, or miss.
- [ ] UI targets produce fixed screen anchors and map targets produce copied
      world anchors.
- [ ] Native or DwarfUI-owned UI cannot accidentally expose an underlying map
      context menu.

## Phase 4 - Own the opening and closing input gestures

- [ ] Add `context_menu/input_hook.lua` with reload-safe hook ownership,
      predecessor preservation, exact restoration, and foreign-wrapper safety.
- [ ] Intercept native viewscreen input at
      `plugins.overlay.feed_viewscreen_widgets()` before delegating to its
      predecessor.
- [ ] Intercept Lua-screen input at the owning screen instance's effective
      `onInput()` before delegating to its predecessor.
- [ ] Install Lua-screen hooks only on roots that can own an eligible
      registered target.
- [ ] On `_MOUSE_R_DOWN`, resolve and latch an eligible target and consume the
      boundary without opening yet.
- [ ] On the matching `_MOUSE_R`, consume the boundary and open the latched
      target.
- [ ] If the runtime delivers only `_MOUSE_R`, resolve, consume, and open from
      that event.
- [ ] Clear a latched opening target if its root, eligibility, pointer
      position, registration generation, or definition becomes invalid before
      completion.
- [ ] Ensure every delivered boundary of an opening gesture is consumed while
      an unregistered miss preserves predecessor calls and exact return values.
- [ ] While a menu is open, consume Escape and close it.
- [ ] While a menu is open, consume the complete second-right-click gesture,
      close once, and suppress its trailing boundary so it cannot reopen a
      target.
- [ ] While a menu is open, consume a left-click outside, close once, and
      suppress any delivered trailing boundary.
- [ ] Route a left-click inside an enabled entry to selection; close and
      consume before invoking its handler.
- [ ] Route keyboard selection through the same close-before-callback path.
- [ ] Prevent handler errors from restoring or duplicating a closed session;
      report the error through the established DFHack error boundary.
- [ ] Add focused hook tests for native and Lua seams, paired and unpaired
      mouse events, misses, blockers, predecessor return preservation,
      reentrancy, reload adoption, exact restoration, and foreign wrappers.

### Phase 4 completion gate

- [ ] Opening, outside-left-click closing, second-right-click closing, Escape,
      and selection each consume their input exactly once.
- [ ] A miss is behaviorally transparent to the predecessor.
- [ ] No half-gesture can leak into native DF, another overlay, or a newly
      opened menu.

## Phase 5 - Implement the interactive menu screen and renderer

- [ ] Add `context_menu/screen.lua` as a short-lived `gui.ZScreen` host owned
      by one open session.
- [ ] Configure the screen so opening a menu does not force or toggle pause.
- [ ] Render the parent first and the context menu last so the menu is the
      topmost final paint.
- [ ] Preserve appropriate parent movement input for an open map-tile menu so
      camera movement can occur and visibly exercise live reprojection.
- [ ] Do not forward Escape, right-click, outside left-click, entry selection,
      or any other context-menu-owned input to the parent.
- [ ] Add `context_menu/renderer.lua` with an optional title and a selectable,
      scrollable entry list.
- [ ] Size width from the longest title or entry label plus frame padding.
- [ ] Cap height to the available screen space and enable wheel and keyboard
      scrolling when entries do not fit.
- [ ] Fill each complete entry row with its resolved background rather than
      coloring only the label cells.
- [ ] Paint each entry with its resolved foreground and background.
- [ ] Define deterministic selected and hovered pens that preserve readable
      contrast when entries use custom colors.
- [ ] Keep the title nonselectable and omit any automatic list-count suffix.
- [ ] Support keyboard navigation and selection, left-click selection, and
      wheel scrolling.
- [ ] Clamp the final menu frame to every screen edge without changing the
      stored source anchor.
- [ ] Recompute layout after interface dimension changes.
- [ ] Dismiss the screen exactly once on selection, explicit close, source
      invalidation, reload, world unload, or owner removal.
- [ ] Add focused renderer and screen tests for empty title, long labels,
      custom pens, selection pens, scrolling, every screen edge, small
      interfaces, resize, and all close paths.

### Phase 5 completion gate

- [ ] The menu is readable, topmost, navigable, and fully interactive with
      both default and entry-specific colors.
- [ ] Screen ownership does not pause the game or pass menu-owned input to the
      parent.
- [ ] Every dismissal path destroys one open screen and one session.

## Phase 6 - Implement screen-position and map-tile placement

- [ ] Keep a widget menu's captured screen anchor fixed while its source
      widget moves or rerenders.
- [ ] Re-clamp a widget menu after screen-size changes without changing its
      captured anchor.
- [ ] For map-tile sessions, retain a copied x/y/z world coordinate and
      re-resolve the current dwarfmode viewport before every render.
- [ ] Use the active DFHack viewport helper for text-mode world-to-screen
      projection.
- [ ] Use the active Premium viewport corner, interface dimensions, and zoom
      factor for graphics-mode projection.
- [ ] Keep the projected anchor and menu frame in one interface coordinate
      space.
- [ ] Reproject after camera panning, zoom, interface resize, and other
      viewport changes.
- [ ] Close and consume no additional input when the tile becomes offscreen,
      changes away from the displayed z-level, the world unloads, or the
      owning registration becomes invalid.
- [ ] Do not pin an offscreen map menu to the nearest screen edge; it would no
      longer appear attached to its source tile.
- [ ] Do not change viewport, cursor, game pause, or native map state merely to
      keep the menu visible.
- [ ] If a generic projection helper is extracted, migrate the existing
      minecart projection to it or prove why two implementations are required;
      do not silently duplicate graphics-mode math.
- [ ] Add unit tests proving a screen-position anchor remains fixed.
- [ ] Add unit tests proving a map anchor moves after viewport changes and
      closes for offscreen, wrong-z, invalid-owner, and world-unload cases.
- [ ] Add text-mode and Premium projection coverage for map edges, zoom,
      interface resize, and clamped menu placement.

### Phase 6 completion gate

- [ ] Widget context menus remain at their captured screen positions.
- [ ] Map context menus visibly track their world tiles every render.
- [ ] Projection invalidation closes cleanly without stale screens, map
      mutation, or input side effects.

## Phase 7 - Integrate lifecycle, reload, registry, packaging, and docs

- [ ] Add `context_menu/service.lua` as the single process-wide owner of the
      active session, opening latch, hook generation, and diagnostics.
- [ ] Enforce at most one active context menu process-wide.
- [ ] Opening a new valid target closes any older session before creating the
      replacement.
- [ ] Make module reload invalidate stale callbacks, latches, registrations,
      screens, and render/input ownership from the prior generation.
- [ ] Restore only hooks owned by this generation and never overwrite a
      foreign wrapper installed after DwarfUI.
- [ ] Clear the active menu and registrations on world unload and DwarfUI
      teardown.
- [ ] Add every reload-managed module to
      `dwarfui/module_registry.lua` in dependency order.
- [ ] Update module-registry tests for load and environment-clear order.
- [ ] Update package-contract tests for all
      `dwarfui/context_menu/` production modules.
- [ ] Update build/package verification so nested production and test
      directories are discovered correctly.
- [ ] Document the public registration, update, unregister, map-handle,
      definition, color-fallback, selection-context, close, and anchoring
      contracts in the project README or a dedicated guide.
- [ ] Include examples for a widget screen-position menu and an exact map-tile
      menu.
- [ ] Document that selection and outside left-click both close and consume.
- [ ] Link `Docs/project.todo` to this checklist without marking the project
      item complete before every definition-of-done gate passes.

### Phase 7 completion gate

- [ ] Reload and teardown leave no stale screen, hook, latch, registration,
      pointer state, or callback.
- [ ] Registry order, package contents, public documentation, and both anchor
      examples match the implemented API.

## Phase 8 - Add native component and interaction coverage

- [ ] Add a DwarfSpec component test for a registered DwarfUI overlay control
      whose context menu opens at the captured screen position.
- [ ] Right-click the actual rendered control through the production input
      boundary.
- [ ] Prove the backing UI does not receive either boundary of the opening
      right-click.
- [ ] Prove an outside left-click closes and does not reach backing UI.
- [ ] Reopen and prove a second right-click closes and does not reopen or reach
      backing UI.
- [ ] Reopen and prove Escape closes and is consumed.
- [ ] Reopen, select an entry with a real left-click, and prove it closes,
      consumes, and calls the handler once.
- [ ] Reopen, select an entry with keyboard input, and prove it closes,
      consumes, and calls the handler once.
- [ ] Add a Lua `gui.ZScreen` component case that opens through its instance
      input seam rather than the native overlay seam.
- [ ] Add a map-tile component case against a real visible same-z map tile.
- [ ] Prove opening the map menu suppresses native map right-click behavior.
- [ ] Move the map camera while the menu remains open and prove the menu moves
      with the same source tile.
- [ ] Change z-level or pan the source tile outside the visible viewport and
      prove the menu closes cleanly.
- [ ] Exercise custom title, menu colors, per-entry overrides, long lists,
      scrolling, and selection in the mounted production renderer.
- [ ] Snapshot and restore pointer, viewport, z-level, pause state, screen
      stack, overlay state, and any test-owned registrations even when an
      assertion fails.
- [ ] Require DwarfSpec `cleanup_confirmed=true` and independently inspect
      retained screens, hooks, registrations, and pointer state.

### Phase 8 completion gate

- [ ] Production widget and map registrations open through their real input
      seams and consume opening, closing, and selection input.
- [ ] The screen-position anchor is fixed and the map-tile anchor tracks camera
      movement in the mounted production system.
- [ ] Cleanup is confirmed with no retained UI, hooks, registrations, or
      changed game state.

## Phase 9 - Complete verification and live acceptance

- [ ] Run the focused definition, registration, detector, hook, renderer,
      screen, service, and projection unit specs through
      `./tools/Run-UnitTests.ps1`.
- [ ] Run the focused context-menu DwarfSpec files through
      `./tools/Run-AutomationTests.ps1`, which remains a direct
      `dwarfspec run` pass-through.
- [ ] Run the complete standalone unit suite.
- [ ] Run the complete DwarfSpec suite.
- [ ] Run `./tools/Check-LuaSyntax.ps1 -IncludeTests`.
- [ ] Run the offline build through `./tools/Build.ps1` without claiming live
      runtime evidence.
- [ ] Run expanded and archive package verification through the scripts under
      `./tools/`.
- [ ] Run `git diff --check`.
- [ ] Install the built package in the configured live DFHack instance and run
      `dwarfui reload`.
- [ ] Confirm the live module registry contains one coherent context-menu
      generation and no stale hook or screen.
- [ ] Manually right-click a registered UI control and confirm the menu opens
      at the click's screen position.
- [ ] Manually confirm opening, outside left-click closing, second-right-click
      closing, Escape, mouse selection, and keyboard selection are consumed
      and do not activate backing UI.
- [ ] Manually right-click a registered map tile and confirm the menu follows
      map panning and zoom.
- [ ] Manually confirm map-tile invalidation on viewport exit and z-level
      change.
- [ ] Review DFHack console output and logs after interaction, reload, world
      unload, and teardown.
- [ ] Record focused unit, complete unit, focused DwarfSpec, complete
      DwarfSpec, syntax, build, package, registry, cleanup, and manual visual
      evidence separately.

### Phase 9 completion gate

- [ ] All automated suites, syntax checks, builds, packages, and whitespace
      checks pass.
- [ ] Live DFHack proves both placement modes and all required consumption and
      closure behavior without Lua errors or stale lifecycle state.
- [ ] No automated registration or cleanup result is reported as visual live
      success.

## Definition of done

- [ ] A caller can register a validated `ContextMenuDefinition` against a UI
      widget or exact map tile.
- [ ] Optional title, menu foreground/background defaults, entry labels,
      entry handlers, and independent entry color overrides behave as
      documented.
- [ ] Widget menus open at the captured screen position and remain fixed there
      while open.
- [ ] Map menus remain attached to their projected world tiles as the camera
      moves and close when the tile is no longer projectable.
- [ ] Every opening right-click is fully consumed.
- [ ] Escape, a second right-click, and an outside left-click close and consume
      without leaking input.
- [ ] Mouse or keyboard item selection closes first, consumes, and invokes the
      selected handler exactly once.
- [ ] UI targets, blocking regions, and map targets obey deterministic
      precedence.
- [ ] Only one menu is open process-wide.
- [ ] All context-menu-owned source and focused test files live in their
      dedicated directories.
- [ ] Reload, world unload, owner removal, and teardown leave no stale screen,
      hook, latch, registration, callback, or pointer state.
- [ ] All new and modified classes and methods have LuaDoc comments.
- [ ] Unit, component, syntax, build, package, live registration, cleanup, and
      manual visual evidence are complete and reported without conflation.

